# GitHub application setup

Create a browser OAuth App with the actual dashboardHostName output as its
HTTPS homepage and the exact githubRedirectUri output as its callback
(`https://HOST/auth/callback`). Store the client secret only in the input vault;
set githubClientId and an explicit organization/team/user allowlist. Admin users
must also satisfy that allowlist. No App installation or OAuth setting is changed
by topology generation.

The webhook secret is required by the existing hosted runtime; it does not
authorize collection or workflow dispatch. Actions evidence acquisition remains
independently governed by the reviewed control policy. No collection App key,
PAT, admission authority or broker credential is granted to the web process.

AGENT-MCP.md documents separate optional Actions bearer-token plus OIDC access.
Browser OAuth does not enable MCP; this profile leaves that endpoint disabled.
